# CR 702.16e, 702.16k: protection from a player prevents all damage that player's objects would deal to the protected
# player, targeted or not - Fiery Confluence's "2 damage to each opponent", chosen three times, targets no one, and each 2
# is prevented. But protection is only about targeting, damage and enchanting (CR 702.16b-e): an effect that does none of
# those still applies. Bot2's Wheel of Fortune has each player discard their hand and draw seven, Bot1 included: Bot1 casts
# Absolute Virtue on turn 1, draws Ancestral Recall on turn 3 and holds it, and the Wheel on turn 4 discards it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Absolute Virtue
Ancestral Recall
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Fiery Confluence
Wheel of Fortune
Island x13

